* Packages

Every Go program is made up of packages.

Programs start running in package ⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000001⟫main⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000002⟫.

This program is using the packages with import paths ⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000003⟫"fmt"⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000004⟫ and ⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000005⟫"math/rand"⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000006⟫.

By convention, the package name is the same as the last element of the import path. For instance, the ⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000007⟫"math/rand"⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000008⟫ package comprises files that begin with the statement ⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000009⟫package`rand⟪GTI18N_f769f12c_000010⟫.

